{"id": "EUVD-2026-103802", "enisaUuid": "e60dcb60-717d-3eb5-8720-e938ec4e5e70", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naudit: fix exe mark UAF in kill_rules()\n\nkill_rules() removes mixed AUDIT_DIR and AUDIT_EXE rules when an audit\ntree is pruned. It drops entry->rule.exe before removing the rule from\nthe RCU-visible filter lists.\n\nAfter a rule has been installed with AUDIT_ADD_RULE, which requires\nCAP_AUDIT_CONTROL, removing the watched directory can race with another\ntask that is still evaluating the rule. In that case, fsnotify can free\nthe executable mark before the reader reaches audit_mark_compare(),\ncausing a use-after-free.\n\nKASAN reports:\n\n    BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in audit_mark_compare+0x8d/0xa0\n\nUnlink the published rules from the RCU-visible lists and retain them\non tree->rules for cleanup. If any rule has an executable mark, wait for\na single RCU grace period before removing the marks and scheduling the\nentries for freeing. Otherwise, call_rcu() already provides the required\ndeferred freeing without a synchronous wait.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:51:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9aee3caeff4dd4126d84f67607b95cec8719b867", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/304960900991157e6883bdf0b39782b690545ee8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88633025f20ba9c32ccdb3efc86eafdf98cb825c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f2cc5462b78559c7628a9f8ac9a9592e7783183a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa650d87a498844060eecb1d336f4d46f4d1b0b3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-73jm-mgrc-fg99", "CVE-2026-98862"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "019fe723-4510-337c-9ce9-fe050052ee99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "01bc7d9c-6f43-3ddc-9e51-10fd3589d782", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.3"}, {"id": "31645aa3-ba33-3004-a452-b68c6850b226", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <aa650d87a498844060eecb1d336f4d46f4d1b0b3"}, {"id": "4cd3eb86-d0a6-3f31-b047-fd377d77cf8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "5829da7f-bef1-3255-b9f1-2f68a0772b29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "5a69a0cf-3894-37cc-b8d7-b2639b7de1f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <9aee3caeff4dd4126d84f67607b95cec8719b867"}, {"id": "75f8b22d-fa85-3f3b-bc53-d3d9808220bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <f2cc5462b78559c7628a9f8ac9a9592e7783183a"}, {"id": "8ace5680-7918-32dc-b511-bff4b6c6bcec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a662847c-5821-3772-99a3-a51a352411f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "cfb2742d-59a1-3699-93e6-9fab43284e6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <304960900991157e6883bdf0b39782b690545ee8"}, {"id": "f62510d1-b01a-3c27-b1cb-fa5c7a137438", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <88633025f20ba9c32ccdb3efc86eafdf98cb825c"}, {"id": "f9a4f064-6caf-3d98-852e-548d0b8bed4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "54d9c4e8-52b6-3f68-a847-0ec3bb043178", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}